    "body": "**Summary**\r\n\r\nThis is a collection of added features and bug fixes encountered when trying to run a Kokkos workload that included the gran/hooke/history pair_style, deform fix, and temp/deform compute.\r\n\r\n* Added brownian/kk pair style\r\n* gran/hooke/history\r\n  * fixed call to virial function: e.g. fx_i was being used instead of fx\r\n  * fixed issue with global virial not calculated correctly\r\n  * might be simpler fix, but this is largely copy+paste from lj/cut/dipole/cut/kk (minus energy)\r\n* npair_kokkos\r\n  * fixed issue where particle pairs were missing \r\n* compute temp/deform\r\n  * fixed host sync issue to correct output\r\n* fix deform\r\n  * fixed a performance regression where host sync only needs to occur in one scenario\r\n  * I believe this is correct based on version before recent refactoring\r\n  * It was a significant performance degradation in the particular workload I’m working with (Loop time of 45 vs. 9 seconds on single A100 GPU)\r\n* gran/hooke/history comm memory leak\r\n  * the prior size of comm array was being checked for growing the array or not\r\n  * this value fluctuates over course of run leading to memory leak causing GPU runs to quickly crash\r\n  * new variable introduced to track largest size of array; stable simulation for millions of steps (i.e. GPU memory usage plateaued)\r\n* I’m withholding a kokkos pairstyle for the time being derived from lubricate\r\n  * The modification to pair_lubricate.cpp/.h can be discarded for now if preferred\r\n\r\n**Related Issue(s)**\r\n\r\nFixes #4219\r\n\r\n**Author(s)**\r\n\r\nChris Knight (ANL)\r\nSuman Chakraborty (Purdue)\r\n\r\n**Licensing**\r\n\r\nBy submitting this pull request, I agree, that my contribution will be included in LAMMPS and redistributed under either the GNU General Public License version 2 (GPL v2) or the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1 (LGPL v2.1).\r\n\r\n**Backward Compatibility**\r\n\r\nNo issues, but this will change results for the better.\r\n\r\n**Implementation Notes**\r\n\r\nSeveral test simulations were validated on Polaris@ALCF comparing energies, forces, and virials for tens of steps as well as comparison of CPU & GPU results from multi-million step simulations.\r\n\r\n**Post Submission Checklist**\r\n\r\n- [ ] The feature or features in this pull request is complete\r\n- [ ] Licensing information is complete\r\n- [ ] Corresponding author information is complete\r\n- [ ] The source code follows the LAMMPS formatting guidelines\r\n- [ ] Suitable new documentation files and/or updates to the existing docs are included\r\n- [ ] The added/updated documentation is integrated and tested with the documentation build system\r\n- [ ] The feature has been verified to work with the conventional build system\r\n- [ ] The feature has been verified to work with the CMake based build system\r\n- [ ] Suitable tests have been added to the unittest tree.\r\n- [ ] A package specific README file has been included or updated\r\n- [ ] One or more example input decks are included\r\n\r\n**Further Information, Files, and Links**\r\n",
